[Derived necessary-condition stack]
  Theorem-level: q=2..13 covered and q=14 omitted; otherwise a q-grid witness
  gives M>1/14, or the denominator-14 apex is blocked.
  Theorem-level: unit residues must be represented; otherwise some a/14 is
  strictly lonely.
  AP/GW fingerprint: cofinite nonzero residue support, maximal antipodal
  zsum, exact odd skeleton, AP complement sums 14, and all residue defect
  lives as zero or one even-shell dipole.
  Strong speculative fingerprint: residue representatives are minimal except
  for one acceleration petal m -> 2m; the only tight petal seen is the top
  one, 12 -> 24.  Other petals survive coarse filters but escape off apex.
  In these banks the full top-petal stack leaves only AP/GW (or AP alone
  when 24 is outside the bank), with no below-threshold row.
